course: dictionary
lesson: 5957
title: Words of praise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When a word is a grand, old-fashioned word of praise, the words around it show how good the thing is. «Won back by matchless valour, consummate strategy, and a proper handling of sticks.» Valour means bravery, consummate means perfect, and strategy means a clever plan, so matchless must mean something very, very good.
explain: Use the swap check: replace matchless with "so good that nothing is equal to it" and see if the sentence still makes sense. It does, so you have the meaning.
explain: Watch out for tone. In The Wind in the Willows, Toad boasts about his own matchless driving, but the reader knows he is far from it. The word can praise something, and it can also be a joke when someone is showing off.
fact: Matchless means so good that nothing or nobody is equal to it.
fact: Matchless is an adjective, a word that describes a noun, such as valour or beauty.
fact: Matchless is a grand, slightly old-fashioned word, and it is mostly used to praise.
fact: In «matchless beauty» and «matchless skill», the word tells you the beauty or skill has no equal.
fact: Toad's boasts about his own matchless driving are funny because the reader knows he is not as good as he claims.
exercise: «Won back by matchless valour, consummate strategy, and a proper handling of sticks.» What does matchless mean here? | Very small and hard to see | Tired and slow | Made of metal | *So good that nothing is equal to it
exercise: Toad boasts of his matchless driving, but the reader knows he is far from it. What does this show? | Toad is the best driver in the world | *Toad is showing off, and the word is a joke | Toad is too shy to drive | Toad has never been in a car
exercise: Which word could replace matchless in «matchless beauty» without changing the meaning much? | *Unequalled | Dull | Noisy | Tiny
test: Is matchless a word of praise or of blame? | Neither, it is a number | Insult | *Praise | Blame
test: What does matchless mean in «matchless skill»? | Skill that is very noisy | Skill that comes from a shop | *Skill that nobody can equal | Skill that makes you sad
exam: Which sentence uses matchless to mean the best? | The matchless dog ran home | He ate a matchless sandwich for lunch | *Her singing was matchless, and nobody in the choir could equal it | The matchless table was brown
